<title>CROATIA: Croatia January M1 falls 6.4 pct, M4 rises 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Croatia January M1 falls 6.4 pct, M4 rises 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Croatia</p>
<p>issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA MONEY SUPPLY	  JANUARY     DEC '96     JAN '96</p>
<p> Reserve money (million HRK) 8,331.3     8,770.3     6,513.5</p>
<p> M1 money supply		10,638.0    11,409.3     8,339.1</p>
<p> Broadest money M4	    37,374.4    36,595.5    25,962.7</p>
<p>NOTE -- January reserve money fell 5.01 percent from December last year and money M1 shrank 6.37 percent. Broadest money, or total liquid assets, rose 2.13 percent on a monthly basis.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
